what this says:
  STATE (can the afference report unobserved substrate?)  cortex +0.5956   ridge +0.4956   MLP -0.2225
  TRAJECTORY (does it predict where the state is going?)  cortex -4.5558   ridge -0.0094   MLP -4.7140
  severing the kernel post hoc costs +0.0183 on state; a permuted kernel RETRAINED reaches +0.4542 (+0.1414 behind trained).
  LUMPING every conduction group onto step 0, keeping all fifteen channels, costs +0.0099 on state.  that is the only arm that tests the DELAY rather than the channels.
  removing every unmyelinated group and retraining costs +0.1811 on state and +21.7378 on trajectory.  those five C-fibre channels are the slow chemical and nociceptive arm, and they are the half of visceral afference that arrives 168-508 ms after the mechanical half.
